1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,088
Look up right now. That burning golden sunset? It is a giant flat lie.

2
00:00:05,388 --> 00:00:13,164
Every single evening at exactly six, the horizon glitches just enough to reveal the cold metal frame.

3
00:00:13,464 --> 00:00:19,992
My grandfather spent his whole life building this crude metal ladder to reach the upper ridge.

4
00:00:20,292 --> 00:00:26,652
The air gets thinner the higher you climb, smelling faintly of hot copper and burnt plastic.

5
00:00:26,952 --> 00:00:34,608
I reach the top edge, press my bare palm against the warm glowing orange atmosphere, and push.

6
00:00:34,908 --> 00:00:43,044
The painted sky peels back like cheap wallpaper, exposing a pitch-black void filled with crawling silver ships.

7
00:00:43,344 --> 00:00:51,168
Down below, my entire town cheerfully eats dinner under the comforting glow of a fake dying sun.

8
00:00:51,468 --> 00:01:01,164
A robotic voice whispers directly into my mind: unauthorized breach detected, resetting visual feed in three seconds.

9
00:01:01,464 --> 00:01:09,696
The rip in the sky heals instantly, plunging me back into the safe, beautiful, deadly golden hour.

10
00:01:09,996 --> 00:01:16,572
Would you rather live inside a comforting lie, or choke on the terrifying truth of the void?
